github.com/samosvalishe/free-turn-proxy). The upstream source file carries:

    // SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT

and that per-file grant is the license under which this code is redistributed
here.

Note on the absence of a copyright line: neither the upstream source file nor
the upstream repository's root LICENSE names a copyright holder. The root
LICENSE is additionally not a plain MIT file -- it is a "Happy Bunny License",
i.e. MIT's text plus the extra condition "You must be kind to bunnies" -- which
is why automated tooling reports that repository as NOASSERTION. MIT's
requirement to preserve a copyright notice is satisfied here as far as it can
be: there is no upstream notice to preserve, so the attribution above stands in
its place.

Local modifications made in this repository (profile auto-detection and a
non-in-place unwrap helper) are marked in the source and are licensed
GPL-3.0-or-later like the rest of this project. MIT is GPL-compatible, so this
combination is permitted; the reverse is not -- do not copy the GPL-3.0 local
additions back upstream without relicensing them.

